  "scenario": "An event-sourced microservice routes commands through a CommandBus to a CommandHandler interface. CreateOrderHandler implements that contract, emits an OrderCreatedEvent (a specialized abstract DomainEvent), and appends it to an EventStore interface.",
  "goal": "Model the full CQRS command-handling pipeline connecting the bus, handler abstraction, concrete handler, domain event hierarchy, and event store.",
  "learningObjective": "Architect a decoupled CQRS pipeline combining Realization, Generalization, and abstraction-based Dependencies.",
  "hints": [
    "CommandBus dispatches through the CommandHandler interface, and CreateOrderHandler implements CommandHandler.",
    "OrderCreatedEvent inherits from the abstract DomainEvent class, while CreateOrderHandler creates OrderCreatedEvent and persists via EventStore.",
    "Connect CommandBus -> CommandHandler (Dependency), CreateOrderHandler -> CommandHandler (Realization), OrderCreatedEvent -> DomainEvent (Generalization), CreateOrderHandler -> OrderCreatedEvent (Dependency), and CreateOrderHandler -> EventStore (Dependency)."
  ],
  "solutionExplanation": "CommandBus depends on the CommandHandler interface. CreateOrderHandler realizes CommandHandler, depends on OrderCreatedEvent (which generalizes DomainEvent), and depends on the EventStore interface to persist events.",
